 "text": "Auditor - Platte County\nElected Officials\nAssessor\nAuditor\nCollector\nCommission\nCounty Clerk\nProsecutor\nPublic Administrator\nRecorder\nSheriff\nEmergency Preparedness\nTreasurer\nDepartments\nState\nBoard of Elections\nCircuit Clerk\nCourts/Judges\nJuvenile Services\nCommission\nFacilities Management\nHuman Resources\nInformation Technology\nParks & Recreation\nPlanning & Zoning\nPublic Works\nVisitors Bureau\nAgendas & Minutes\nPlatte County\nCounty News\nAbout Us\nOur Community\nServices\nTaxes & Licenses\nSchools\nRecord Requests\nHousehold Hazardous Waste\nGet Involved\nCounty Board Appointments\nCounty In Action\nEmployment Opportunities\nImportant Links\nFacility Use Indemnification Agreement\nContact Us\nCounty Contacts\nCounty Holidays\nWho To Contact\nMy Profile\nSign Up\nLogin\nPlatte County Auditor's Office\nElected Officeholder: Kevin Robinson\nPlatte County Administration Building\n415 Third St., Room 112\nPlatte City, MO 64079\nPhone: (816) 858-3328\nResponsibilities\nPrepares the annual budget for approval by the County Commission.\nInventories all County-owned property.\nApproves all disbursements of funds.\nAudits monthly financial reports.\nMaintains the County's accounting system.\nElected Officeholder: Kevin Robinson\nPlatte County Administration Building\n415 Third St., Room 112\nPlatte City, MO 64079\nPhone: (816) 858-3328\nResponsibilities\nPrepares the annual budget for approval by the County Commission.\nInventories all County-owned property.\nApproves all disbursements of funds.\nAudits monthly financial reports.\nMaintains the County's accounting system.\nPlatte County Auditor's Office\nParent Page\nNo content items.\nAuditor Forms Proposed Budget Amendments\nAuditor's Office\nKevin Robinson\nAuditor\n(816) 858-3327\nKevin Robinson\nAuditor\n(816) 858-3327\nPlatte County Auditor, J. Kevin Robinson, MBA, was elected in 2010. He brings diverse experience and leadership background to the Auditor’s Office with twenty plus years of executive management experience and business ownership. His leadership was instrumental in Platte County’s 2011 Going Green Initiative, and his audit experience has proven invaluable in launching compliance audits throughout the County; ensuring proper cash handling and transaction recording procedures.\nKevin has proven himself to be a community leader by sharing his knowledge and experience with college students, and by donating his services to various Boards of Directors; including, the Northland Regional Chamber of Commerce, State Professional Associations, Maple Woods Community College Academic Advisory Board, Platte City Area Chamber and Economic Development Commission, and Kansas City International Rotary Club and Scholarship Foundation.\nAuditor's Office Home\nServices\nAnnual Financial Statements\nType : CommonServices\nMonthly Financial Statements\nType : CommonServices\nBudget Documents\nType : CommonServices\nCompliance Audits\nType : CommonServices\nOpen Finance\nType : CommonServices\nAuditor Miscellaneous\nType : CommonServices\nAuthorized Department\nNo content items.\nFalse\nServices\nAnnual Financial Statements\nMonthly Financial Statements\nBudget Documents\nCompliance Audits\nOpen Finance\nAuditor Miscellaneous\nShare\nContact Us\nCounty Courthouse and Administrative Building 415 Third Street\nPlatte City, MO 64079\nHours of operation\nMon-Fri 8:00 am - 5:00 pm\nCounty Phone Number\nMain line: 816-858-2232\nCounty Facebook\nPlatte County\nParks and Recreation\nCounty Twitter\nPlatte County\nCounty Youtube\nPlatte County\nSitemap\nSite Terms and Privacy Policy\nPowered by MCCi Government Websites",
